   "explain": {
    "en": {
     "text": "To reach the nth term, start at G₁ and multiply by r one time fewer than n: Gₙ = G₁ rⁿ⁻¹. From two terms, divide them: the G₁ cancels and you get a power of r. An even power gives two roots, ± ."
